# oracle: fix brownian draws its random numbers in native's local atom order. Native sorts the atoms at setup
#   (atom_modify sort, default every 1000 steps) and its initial_integrate (src/BROWNIAN/fix_brownian.cpp at b332f28)
#   loops over them in that order, so each atom gets native's draws; the engine looped in creation order. The sum of the
#   squared noise does not depend on the pairing, so Temp matched without forces, but the force-noise cross term did
#   not (examples/PACKAGES/brownian/align_self: Temp 3.7e-3 off at step 1000).
# oracle-compare: thermo=all rel=1e-9 abs=1e-12
units           lj
dimension       2
boundary        p p p
atom_style      ellipsoid
region          box block 0 30 0 30 -0.5 0.5
create_box      1 box
create_atoms    1 random 600 12345 box
pair_style      soft 1.122
pair_coeff      * * 33.0
fix             1 all brownian 0.0001 12345 gamma_t 1.0
thermo_style    custom step temp epair press
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          5
run             20
